# AGENTS notes

## Stack
- Python `3.12` (`.python-version`).
- Use `uv` as the package manager.
- Use `hatchling` as the package builder.
- Single-package `src/` layout: importable code lives in `src/lego_lang
- Console entrypoint is `{{project_name}}.lower()`, which calls `{{module_name}}:main`.

## Project Intent
- {{project_intent}}

## Coding Rules
- Follow clean code rules.
- Prefer short functions; target a maximum of 5 lines when practical.
- Avoid more than 2 levels of indentation.
- Use clear, intention-revealing names.
- Keep files short and focused.
- Always provide type annotations.
- Document functions and classes with single line docstrings.

## Testing Rules
- Prefer tests that verify externally observable behavior rather than implementation details.
- Unit tests should be in `tests/` and focus on individual functions or classes.
- Always provide type annotations.
- Use tests doubles in order of dummy, fake, stub, mock, spy, and then real objects as a last resort.
- Use dependency injection to enable test doubles and avoid global state when practical.
- Avoid monkeypatching or patching in tests; prefer explicit test doubles and fixtures.
- Use `pytest` markers to categorize tests, e.g. `@pytest.mark.slow` or `@pytest.mark.component`. When tests need to do file io or network access, or heavy computation.

## Documentation Rules
- Keep documentation up to date with code changes.
- Use Markdown files for documentation placed in `docs/`.
- Use the `README.md` to provide high-level project information, setup instructions, and usage details.
- For large changes to the repo, ask to write an ADR to document the decision and its rationale. Place it in `docs/adr/`

## Verification Commands
- Install dev dependencies in the generated project with `uv sync --dev`.
- Run unit tests with `uv run pytest`.
- Run component tests with `uv run pytest -m component`.
- Run slow tests with `uv run pytest -m slow`.
- Run type checking with `uv run mypy src`.
- Run the same repo hooks users will hit with `uv run pre-commit run --all-files`.
